Conan Exiles build 5.6.1-373004 relocated two engine functions that Pippi 4.0.6 calls. The mod still looks for them at their old address, finds nothing, and the game dies instantly. Four eight-byte values in the mod's cooked data repair it.

Funcom added Stable ID variants of the character and inventory loaders. Rather than duplicate the result-handling logic into the new classes, they hoisted it into a shared base class. The functions were not deleted and not renamed — the names are byte-identical. They changed owner.


<div class="tree">
    <div class="panel tree-before">
      <p class="panel-label">Before — what Pippi 4.0.6 was built against</p>
<pre>LoadInventoryCallProxy
  ├─ LoadInventory
  └─ <span class="broken">ProcessInventoryData</span>

LoadCharacterCallProxy
  ├─ LoadCharacter
  ├─ LoadCharacterWithController
  ├─ LoadCharacterWithUserId
  ├─ LoadNPC
  └─ <span class="broken">ProcessCharacterData</span></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="panel tree-after">
      <p class="panel-label">After — 5.6.1-373004</p>
<pre>LoadInventoryProxyBase
  ├─ <span class="fixed">ProcessInventoryData</span>
  └─ ProcessInventoryDataStableId
     ├─ LoadInventoryCallProxy
     └─ LoadInventoryStableIdCallProxy

LoadCharacterProxyBase
  ├─ <span class="fixed">ProcessCharacterData</span>
  └─ ProcessNPCData
     ├─ LoadCharacterCallProxy
     └─ LoadCharacterByStableIdCallProxy</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
